# Never line-ending-convert the data payloads.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true, checkout was rewriting havc/data.json to CRLF, adding
# one byte per line — 477,516 bytes — which inflated the working copy from
# 24.62 MiB to 25.08 MiB and pushed it past the Cloudflare Workers 25 MiB
# per-asset hard limit. Production was unaffected (git stores LF, and that is
# what gets deployed), but `wrangler dev` refused to start locally.
#
# JSON has no business being CRLF-converted in either direction.
*.json -text

# Same reasoning for the rest of the shipped text surface: these are served
# byte-for-byte over HTTP, so the repo and the wire should agree.
*.js   -text
*.css  -text
*.html -text
*.svg  -text

# Config files parsed line-by-line. A CRLF checkout would leave a trailing \r on
# every .assetsignore pattern, which would silently stop the exclusions matching.
*.jsonc        -text
*.sql          -text
.assetsignore  -text
.gitattributes -text
.gitignore     -text
